  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Targeted HIV Prevention and Community-Based Diagnosis, Treatment and Care &amp; Support in Mobility-Impacted Communities in Mon &amp; Kayin States</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IOM will continue to support the NAP in comprehensively addressing HIV amongst Key Affected Populations (KAP) and other priority groups including migrants and mobile populations in mobility impacted high priority communities, border areas, and economic corridors in Myanmar. IOM will engage with Mon- and Kayin- based CBOs. IOM will provide capacity building and technical support to its partners to implement HIV prevention services packages for KAP. IOM will improve its current programming through localization, via the partnership with Mon- and Kayin- based CBOs, and continued partnership with Karen Department of Health Welfare (KDWH) to extend HIV and TB integrated services to underserved ethnic minority populations.</narrative>
  </description>
